    "title": "San Antonio restaurant near the top of Yelp's 100 best in U.S. list - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rhyma Castillo ,\n9 hours ago Aside from supporting addiction treatment through the SerenityStar Recovery program, Yelp praised the restaurant for delivering \"unbridled peak breakfast greatness,\" quoting one patron's review. (Mike Sutter/San Antonio Express-News) Since opening in San Antonio in May 2019, Comfort Café has been recognized repeatedly as one of the city's best breakfast spots. Now in 2026, the \"pay-what-you-can\" nonprofit eatery has earned high marks on a nationally recognized foodie hotlist.\nYelp just dropped its 13th annual Top 100 U.S. Restaurants list for 2026, \"the highest-reviewed restaurants, diners, fast-casual spots, food halls, and more — all ranked by the Yelp community.\"\nComfort Café landed right near the tippy top, at No. 5 in the country.\nSo, what makes Comfort Café so special? Aside from supporting addiction treatment through the SerenityStar Recovery program, Yelp praised the restaurant for delivering \"unbridled peak breakfast greatness,\" quoting one patron's review .\nALSO READ: Restaurants Near Me: New map of San Antonio’s best places to eat\nThe Lone Star Breakfast at Comfort Cafe on Bandera Road. (Mike Sutter/San Antonio Express-News) The review site highlighted a few fan-favorite menu items, such as the \"fluffy\" and \"melt-in-your-mouth\" brown sugar pecan pancakes, the Alamo Benny with chipotle Hollandaise sauce, as well as the San Antonio burger — which comes \"with a beef-chorizo patty topped with cheese, bacon, a fried egg, and chipotle mayo.\"\nIn June 2024, Comfort Café's Bandera kitchen manager Justin Motl said the restaurant staff uses seasonal ingredients to keep things fresh.\nALSO READ: Chacho’s restaurants’ ownership facing new fraud allegations\n\"We get to use our creativity; we get to play with different ingredients,\" he told the Express-News. \"We try to stay seasonal, using what’s fresh,\" he said. The restaurant almost exclusively employs people who either have completed or are working through SerenityStar's 12-step addiction recovery program, he noted.\n\"The people that are actually in the program are in the kitchen, and they're the ones who get to do those specials,\" Motl said.\nThe nonprofit's focus on recovery plays out every weekend at Comfort Café's flagship location at 6812 Bandera Road, which is is open from 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays.\nALSO READ: On this Bexar County farm, all the dogs live happily ever after\nThe menu at Comfort Cafe sometimes includes a special pancake flight with three different toppings. (Mike Sutter/San Antonio Express-News) Sign up for San Antonio Express-News newsletters here\nRead the original article on expressnews.com\n3",
